      "math_academy_id": "e-4789",
      "problem": "Find $s,$ if $3\\mathbf{a_1}+s\\mathbf{a_2} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14244365/assets/a5b94b07dbcb3febbcb1b9e9b034386976d0c42d4839b04609b66af70434e8f8.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $s$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+s{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $s=4.$",
